{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Every firstborn of a donkey.</b> And not the firstborn of other unclean animals; it is a decree of Scripture, because the firstborn of Egypt were likened to donkeys; and further, because they assisted Israel in their departure — for there is not one of Israel who did not take many donkeys from Egypt, laden with the silver and gold of Egypt." "<b>You shall redeem with a lamb.</b> He gives a lamb to the priest, and the firstborn donkey is permitted for benefit, and the lamb is unconsecrated in the priest's hand (Bekhorot 9)." "<b>You shall break its neck.</b> He breaks its neck with a cleaver from behind and kills it; he deprived the priest of his money — therefore he loses his own money (ibid. 10)." "<b>And every firstborn of man among your sons you shall redeem.</b> Five shekels is the fixed amount of his redemption, stated elsewhere (Numbers 18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {2 "קופיץ rendered 'cleaver'; Rashi's term refers to a hatchet or chopper used for slaughter from behind."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:57.929732447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}